; coverage test for numbers.kurt's factorial recursion, added alongside "factorial-base"
; (previously the only factorial fact, `0! = 1`, with no recursive step at all -- `n!` for any
; n != 0 was simply not derivable from anything). Proves `1! = 1` by chaining
; "factorial-step" + "factorial-base" + "mul-identity".
;
; note: chaining a *second* application of "factorial-step" used to fail, since substituting
; `1! = 1 * 1` into `2 * 1!` needs to rewrite the group `1 * 1` inside the flat `2 * 1 * 1` --
; equal-elim can do that now, see proofs/debug/flat-group-rewrite.kurt. The literal
; arithmetic (`1 - 1 = 0`) still has to be stated, since `calc` doesn't compute while matching
; an axiom's pattern (`($n - 1)!` against `0!`).
load numbers
use 1 - 1 = 0   "lit-1-1"
use 1 > 0

show 1! = 1
proof
    1! = 1 * (1-1)!
       = 1 * 0!
       = 1 * 1
       = 1
qed
